event('190-2b-finite-exactness','targeted proof check','Checked the kernel-pair specialization and affine formula. For finite alpha with A injected in B, the map on spaces is closed and surjective. Equality of two maps after alpha therefore determines their underlying maps, and injectivity of O_S into alpha_*O_S-prime determines their sheaf maps. If A=Eq(B => B tensor_A B), an invariant map out of S-prime factors topologically through the closed quotient S, and its sheaf maps descend by the equalizer on inverse images of affine opens. Conversely affine targets recover the algebra equalizer. The general pair beta1,beta2 requires the finite quotient argument and remains a background input.','190, pp. 305–306, finite exactness criterion')
event('190-2b-finite-epi-example','computation or formal certificate','Computed the equalizer over Q for B=Q[t]/(t^8) and A=span(1,t^4,t^5,t^6). A Groebner remainder calculation gave nonzero independent deltas in degrees 1,2,3 and zero deltas in degrees 4,5,6,7. The elementary exact identity delta7=(x+y)delta6-xy delta5 is preserved in scripts/check_190_finite_epi.py. Thus E=span(1,t^4,t^5,t^6,t^7) is the equalizer, strictly larger than A: Spec B -> Spec A is a finite epimorphism but not strict, with Artinian local base.','190, p. 306, paragraph after the affine equalizer')
event('190-2b-strict-composition','targeted proof check','For the preceding A subset E subset B, B tensor_A B equals B tensor_E B since delta(t^7) is already zero; hence Spec B -> Spec E is strict. E -> A has the ring retraction killing t^7 and fixing A, so Spec E -> Spec A is a split, hence strict, epimorphism. Their composite is not strict. Further, quotient E by (t^4,t^5,t^6) leaves a nonzero t^7, whereas B tensor_E E/(t^4,t^5,t^6)=B/(t^4) kills it; this base change is not even an epimorphism. This checks the warning that finite strict epimorphisms need not be descent morphisms.','190, p. 306, composition and flatness warnings')
event('190-2b-finite-factorization','carried as background without fault found','Read the asserted finite factorization over a noetherian prescheme. No general proof was reconstructed here. The explicit Artinian example above admits the required two-step factorization, but does not establish the general assertion; a finite strict-closure/factorization argument is still needed.','190, p. 306, underlined factorization assertion')
event('190-2c-flat-base-change','targeted proof check','Tensoring the sheaf equalizer 0 -> A -> B -> C with a flat algebra preserves its kernel, so flat base change preserves the finite exact diagram. Applying this to X -> S makes X a coequalizer of X-double-prime => X-prime and gives the displayed Hom equalizer; epimorphy ensures the descended map is over S. For flat quasi-coherent M, tensoring gives M as the equalizer of its two pullbacks; compatible module maps descend into this equalizer. No flatness of the target of a morphism is needed for this Hom argument.','190, p. 306, section 2(c)')
event('190-2.3-finite-four-distinct','refuted, with the refined statement\x27s id','Candidate refinement 190-2.3-finite-universal-coincidence: for a finite morphism, universal epimorphy implies universal strict epimorphy. Locally A -> B is universally injective; testing A-algebras A direct-sum M with square-zero M makes M -> M tensor_A B injective for every module M. If b tensor 1=1 tensor b, take M=B/A and quotient the first factor: the class of b maps to zero in M tensor B, hence is zero. Thus A is the equalizer, and the argument persists after every base change. This conflicts with the literal four-distinct-even-finite wording on p. 305. Retained the historical assertion pending the ordered errata/notes review; not treated as a visually identifiable typo or silently rewritten.','190, pp. 305–306, four notions and finite equalizer criterion')
record_page('190',306,r'''Compared sources/fr_printed/fr/190.tex and sources/fr/fr/190.tex entry lines 384–437 with scan leaf 9 at 400 dpi, full page and three enlarged bands. Read all algebra/sheaf diagrams, tensor subscripts, affine criterion, the factorization assertion and the Hom diagram. The marker is correctly before de platitude in the next-page continuation.

Restored the omitted alpha label on the first algebra arrow, wavy-underlined O and A versus plain affine ring letters, wavy C, hyphenated pré-schéma, the factorization statement underlining, four individual flatness underlines, c. without dash, and the printed commas and parenthesis punctuation. No French-layer mathematical difference was introduced on this page.

Checked the affine strict-epimorphism criterion and its geometric kernel-pair interpretation. Constructed the explicit Artinian example A=Q+Qt^4+Qt^5+Qt^6 inside Q[t]/(t^8); its strict equalizer adds t^7. Recorded the exact polynomial identity, a two-step strict factorization with non-strict composite, and a base change destroying even epimorphy. The general noetherian finite-factorization assertion remains background. Verified flat-base-change exactness and the Hom consequence. Also recorded a proof that, for finite morphisms, universal epimorphy implies universal strict epimorphy, flagging the literal four-distinct wording on 305 for the later errata/notes review rather than silently altering the historical claim.''')
